<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="75aed8dc-3a64-5529-8307-20c67bd8990f" activityNameId="747529e6-3c22-52a2-9288-22319b925934" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">CZ single crystalline silicon, photovoltaics, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: CZ single crystalline silicon, photovoltaics, at plant
Solar-grade silicon demand estimated at 1 kg/kg. Electricity demand updated for 2018. The remaining production efforts remain unchanged because recent data were not available.;
CAS number: 7440-21-3; 
Formula: Si; 
Synonyms: Czochralski process; 
UUID: 576fa11b-8bfc-3c19-9cad-f89989713201
Gate to gate inventory for an improved Czochralski process. Crushing of Si, etching with HNO3, HF and acetic acid. Melting in a silica pot and crystallisation to produce a monocrystalline material. Water emissions roughly estimated. Process emissions to air are not known.
Location: Data for RER.
Technology: Czochralski process for production of monocrystalline silicon blocks. Than edges are sliced and blocks are sawn.
Time period: Most data are published in 2006. Electricity demand updated for 2018. Some older data published in 1992.
Production volume: Approximately 105000 MW for total c-Si in 2018
Sampling: Publication of plant specific (partly aggregated) data and literature information. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_576fa11b-8bfc-3c19-9cad-f89989713201.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
